# Docs metadata: README tables, SECURITY table and the "At a glance" box are generated from
# this (dev/gen-docs.py). One "key: value" per line.
emoji: 🗣️
name: Speech engine (helper)
group: helper
what: Gives the Frame a voice: Piper (offline, natural) for Screen snip's Narrate, and espeak-ng for Orca and other apps that speak through speech-dispatcher. Installed automatically.
why: SteamOS ships speech-dispatcher and its espeak-ng module, but not espeak-ng itself, so nothing can speak (the Screen reader's Orca was silent).
changes: Piper and a voice in `~/.local/share/frame-tweaks/speech` (checksum-pinned), `~/.config/speech-dispatcher/speechd.conf` (backed up, restored on uninstall)
access: None beyond your home folder
survives-updates: Yes (everything is in your home folder)
undo: `./install.sh uninstall speech` (after Screen snip and Screen reader)
